# --- never commit a documentation corpus -------------------------------------
# The skills build a local copy of docs.dynatrace.com for personal reference.
# That copy is not ours to redistribute. These patterns are deliberately broad:
# a corpus accidentally committed is far harder to undo than a false positive.
docs/
developer/
corpus/
_reports/
*.corpus/
**/all-doc-paths.txt

# Derived indexes — rebuilt by the corpus tooling, never commit.
# They embed another site's structure and go stale the moment it moves.
section-index.tsv
ui-map.tsv
ui-topography.md
page-hashes.tsv
image-index.tsv

# --- local setup -------------------------------------------------------------
# Nothing here should carry a real corpus path. The skill reads $DT_DOCS and
# $DT_DEV from the environment, so there is no config file to leak — these
# patterns only guard against someone adding one.
config.json
config.local.json
*.local

# --- editor and tooling ------------------------------------------------------
.obsidian/
.vscode/
.idea/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
venv/

# --- os ----------------------------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
